From: MacGameFix
Subject: kernelbase, kernel32: FindPackagesByPackageFamily, with no packages to find

Wine has GetPackagesByPackageFamily, which says no package is installed, and left
FindPackagesByPackageFamily out: kernelbase.spec had it as a commented stub and kernel32
did not export it. A program that looks it up by name refuses to go on without it.

EA SPORTS FC 27 (Steam, 1.0.142.20665) on NotProton's runner for CrossOver Preview 41303,
2026-11-23: its activation log, ProgramData\Origin\Logs\FC27_16425884_OnlineActivation_Log.html,
says "License signature is good." and then "Missing DLL: KERNEL32.dll Function:
FindPackagesByPackageFamily", four starts of four, and the game ends at the dialog "There
is a problem with your game's setup. Please reinstall your game."

It answers as GetPackagesByPackageFamily does: no packages, ERROR_SUCCESS.

--- a/dlls/kernelbase/version.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/version.c
@@ -1660,6 +1660,29 @@
 }
 
 /***********************************************************************
+ *         FindPackagesByPackageFamily   (kernelbase.@)
+ *
+ * No packages are installed here, as GetPackagesByPackageFamily says too. A program that
+ * looks the function up by name and does not find it can refuse to start: EA SPORTS FC 27's
+ * activation logs "Missing DLL: KERNEL32.dll Function: FindPackagesByPackageFamily" and the
+ * game ends with "There is a problem with your game's setup" (2026-11-23).
+ */
+LONG WINAPI DECLSPEC_HOTPATCH FindPackagesByPackageFamily(const WCHAR *family_name, UINT32 filters, UINT32 *count,
+                                                          WCHAR **full_names, UINT32 *buffer_len, WCHAR *buffer,
+                                                          UINT32 *properties)
+{
+    FIXME( "(%s %#x %p %p %p %p %p): stub\n", debugstr_w(family_name), filters, count, full_names,
+           buffer_len, buffer, properties );
+
+    if (!count || !buffer_len)
+        return ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER;
+
+    *count = 0;
+    *buffer_len = 0;
+    return ERROR_SUCCESS;
+}
+
+/***********************************************************************
  *         GetPackagePathByFullName   (kernelbase.@)
  */
 LONG WINAPI GetPackagePathByFullName(const WCHAR *name, UINT32 *len, WCHAR *path)
--- a/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/kernelbase.spec
@@ -380,7 +380,7 @@
 @ stdcall FindNextFileW(long ptr)
 @ stdcall FindNextStreamW(long ptr)
 @ stdcall FindNextVolumeW(long ptr long)
-# @ stub FindPackagesByPackageFamily
+@ stdcall FindPackagesByPackageFamily(wstr long ptr ptr ptr ptr ptr)
 @ stdcall FindResourceExW(long wstr wstr long)
 @ stdcall FindResourceW(long wstr wstr)
 @ stdcall FindStringOrdinal(long wstr long wstr long long)
--- a/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
+++ b/dlls/kernel32/kernel32.spec
@@ -514,6 +514,7 @@
 @ stdcall -import FindNextVolumeW(long ptr long)
 @ stdcall -import FindNLSString(long long wstr long wstr long ptr)
 @ stdcall -import FindNLSStringEx(wstr long wstr long wstr long ptr ptr ptr long)
+@ stdcall FindPackagesByPackageFamily(wstr long ptr ptr ptr ptr ptr) kernelbase.FindPackagesByPackageFamily
 @ stdcall FindResourceA(long str str)
 @ stdcall FindResourceExA(long str str long)
 @ stdcall -import FindResourceExW(long wstr wstr long)
